    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d653">

                <pb facs="0805" n="731" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg731"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.51/225</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Francis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Petrograd</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-10-14T19:00:00+03:31">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 14, 1917, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received October 19, 5.15
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1864.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>Impressed Roumanian Minister, often also Vopicka, with the necessity of having Washington authorized
                    agent to sign obligations. Angelescu,
                    Roumanian Minister to United States, whom I urged to go direct to Washington
                    instead of stopping in London two weeks, as planned, as did Vopicka when both were here September 8. Allied
                        <pb facs="0806" n="732" xml:id="pg732"/> Ambassadors had three meetings on
                    Roumanian needs, another Tuesday. Shall cable conclusion when reached.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
